            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid, no, not really. There is built-in [`:h diff`](https://neovim.io/doc/user/diff.html#diff) that can show the differences. For me an overlay feels more practical.\r\n\r\n> I marked mini.git as well, tho I am looking to display diffs from jj instead\r\n\r\nI am yet to embark on exploring `jj`, but there is a feeling that some sort of 'mini.nvim' is possible in the future.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid, no, not really. There is built-in <a href=\"https://neovim.io/doc/user/diff.html#diff\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:h diff</code></a> that can show the differences. For me an overlay feels more practical.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I marked mini.git as well, tho I am looking to display diffs from jj instead</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am yet to embark on exploring <code class=\"notranslate\">jj</code>, but there is a feeling that some sort of 'mini.nvim' is possible in the future.</p>",
            "bodyText": "I am afraid, no, not really. There is built-in :h diff that can show the differences. For me an overlay feels more practical.\n\nI marked mini.git as well, tho I am looking to display diffs from jj instead\n\nI am yet to embark on exploring jj, but there is a feeling that some sort of 'mini.nvim' is possible in the future.",
