                    "body": "> So you would strongly recommend checking it out?\r\n\r\nYeah, I'd say so. I've been using it for about three years now (according to my dotfiles) and it is very convenient. Beware that it needs *some* time to get used to. Take a look at [feature demos](https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit?tab=readme-ov-file#features) and maybe tutorials on the Internet to squeeze the most out of it.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So you would strongly recommend checking it out?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yeah, I'd say so. I've been using it for about three years now (according to my dotfiles) and it is very convenient. Beware that it needs <em>some</em> time to get used to. Take a look at <a href=\"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit?tab=readme-ov-file#features\">feature demos</a> and maybe tutorials on the Internet to squeeze the most out of it.</p>",
